ReXGlue codegen: keep reading an absolute jump table past zero entries (holes).

detectJumpTable() ended a table at its first zero entry. MSVC-built Xbox 360 code leaves zeros
for switch cases it knows are never taken: 007: Quantum of Solace's asset-type size switch
(sub_821C1B90, table 0x825E81B8) has 39 entries with zeros at 20 and 29-32, so only types 0-19
were generated and type 26 hit the default __builtin_trap() (illegal instruction, 0xC000001D).

A zero after at least one valid entry is now kept as a hole (a trapping case, as the existing
null-padding sentinel) and reading continues; without bounds the table still ends at the first
non-zero entry that isn't code, and zeros left at the end are dropped. Tables without holes come
out as before. Applies after 0001.

diff --git a/src/codegen/function_scanner.cpp b/src/codegen/function_scanner.cpp
index 52bf329..3c983f2 100644
--- a/src/codegen/function_scanner.cpp
+++ b/src/codegen/function_scanner.cpp
@@ -1805,6 +1805,18 @@ std::optional<JumpTable> detectJumpTable(DecodedBinary& decoded, uint32_t bctrAd
       break;
     }
 
+    // A zero entry after valid ones is a hole: a case the compiler knew was never taken (an
+    // unused value in an enum switch, e.g. 007: Quantum of Solace's asset-type tables, with holes
+    // at 20 and 29-32 of 39). Keep reading; the hole becomes a trapping case, and zeros left at
+    // the end of the table are dropped below. Without bounds, the table still ends at the first
+    // non-zero entry that isn't code.
+    if (target == 0 && tableType == JumpTableType::kAbsolute && !jt.targets.empty()) {
+      REXCODEGEN_TRACE("detectJumpTable: bctr=0x{:08X} entry[{}] is 0: hole, reading on", bctrAddr,
+                       i);
+      jt.targets.push_back(0);
+      continue;
+    }
+
     // Validate target is within code region - jump table targets help DEFINE function extent
     // Don't constrain by funcEnd since that's just PDATA which may not include out-of-line code
     if (target == 0 || !containingRegion.contains(target)) {
@@ -1856,6 +1868,11 @@ std::optional<JumpTable> detectJumpTable(DecodedBinary& decoded, uint32_t bctrAd
     jt.targets.push_back(target);
   }
 
+  // Holes at the end aren't part of the table (padding before whatever follows it).
+  while (!jt.targets.empty() && jt.targets.back() == 0) {
+    jt.targets.pop_back();
+  }
+
   if (jt.targets.empty()) {
     REXCODEGEN_TRACE(
         "detectJumpTable: bctr=0x{:08X} table=0x{:08X} NO VALID TARGETS (funcStart=0x{:08X} "
